---
// DIA for 1.3: what needs the internet once (setup), what never does (daily use), and what always will.
---
<figure class="cs-fig wt">
  <span class="cs-figtag">Diagram</span>
  <div class="wt-grid">
    <section class="wt-col wt-once"><h4>Online, once</h4><ul><li>Download the app (about 0.1 to 1 GB)</li><li>Download one or more models (about 2 to 80 GB each)</li><li>Updates, when you choose</li></ul></section>
    <div class="wt-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
    <section class="wt-col wt-off"><h4>Offline, every day</h4><ul><li>Your questions and the answers</li><li>Your files and documents</li><li>Code, summaries, translations</li></ul><p>Nothing leaves the machine.</p></section>
  </div>
  <section class="wt-col wt-always"><h4>Still needs the internet</h4><ul><li>Searching the web or reading live news</li><li>Sending email or messages for you</li><li>Getting a newer model</li></ul></section>
  <figcaption>"Offline" means the thinking happens on your machine. Getting the files there, and anything that has to reach the outside world, still needs a connection.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .wt-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; align-items: stretch; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  @media (min-width: 620px) { .wt-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; } }
  .wt-arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 26px; color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 619px) { .wt-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); } }
  .wt-col { border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 14px; border: 1.5px solid var(--line); }
  .wt-col h4 { margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .wt-col ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .wt-col p { margin: 6px 0 0; font-weight: 700; color: var(--good); font-size: 15px; }
  .wt-once { border-color: var(--warn); background: var(--warn-soft); }
  .wt-off { border-color: var(--good); background: var(--good-soft); }
  .wt-always { border-style: dashed; }
</style>
